ly due to lack of fever progression and systemic inflammatory markers", "Alcoholic hepatitis: possible but does not explain acute hemodynamic compromise", "Appendicitis: typically right lower quadrant pain with different exam patterns", "Splenic infarction: could explain left-sided pain but not the RUQ focus", "Exercise-induced rhabdomyolysis: possible but unlikely to cause RUQ pain or hypotension"], "alarm_features": ["Hemodynamic instability (hypotension/tachycardia)", "Sudden acute exacerbation during physical activity"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Gynecologic / Pelvic Source of Hemodynamic Instability", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.34090909090909083, "posterior": 0.4137613990535871, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Alcohol use and weight loss provide weak support for alcoholic pancreatitis (B4) and other branches."], "evidence_against": ["Lack of pelvic findings and pending β-hCG weakly argue against gynecologic causes (B1)."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3", "B1.4"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.85, "interrupt_relevance": 0.95, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "anatomy", "representative_diseases": []}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Hepatic / Hepatobiliary Vascular Abnormality", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.34090909090909094, "posterior": 0.09916488132314266, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Alcohol use and weight loss provide weak support for alcoholic pancreatitis (B4) and other branches."], "evidence_against": ["Features suggesting PCOS/Cushing's weakly argue against acute hepatobiliary vascular issues (B2)."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B2.1", "B2.2", "B2.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.5, "diagnosis_com